# Reverse-engineered from ./backup.rhai; the spec twin of ./../service/backup.sdd —
# keep the two texts in lockstep on any lane change.

Spec: TenantBackupScript

Platform: Rhai script library (vynil-core 0.7.7 engine)

Purpose:
  Orchestrate the immediate (no schedule branch exists here) restic backup of one tenant
    package inside a dispatched backup Pod: decode the Pod's own process env into the args map
    via @ctx::from_args, then walk a fixed @import_run stage sequence — pre-hook, restic repo
    init, maintenance-start, the five prepare engines in secret → postgresql → mysql → mongodb
    → redis order, restic backup, maintenance-stop, repo check, post-hook — where one package
    script can replace the whole lane and each prepare engine can be individually replaced by
    its own package script. No CR is ever in hand: the instance is invisible at this level
    (frozen by /agent/src/tenant/backup.sdd), no status/condition/tag is written here, and the
    failure surface is exactly eight @throw strings over custom-script return codes plus
    whatever the stages re-throw. Standalone twin of ./../service/backup.sdd: a real
    `diff -u` of the two sources shows exactly one hunk (`@@ -45,6 +45,22 @@`, +16/−0)
    adding the mongodb then redis prepare legs after the mysql leg — otherwise the files
    are byte-for-byte this flow.

Exposes:
  @run(@args) — the module's sole @fn and entry point (`backup.rhai` + `run` match the
    entry-point patterns of /agent/src/linting/rhai_checker.sdd); invoked as
    `backup::run(args)` by the Rust lane /agent/src/tenant/backup.sdd, whose fixed snippet
    discards the returned @Dynamic.

Accepts:
  @args — the ten-key CLI `args` map injected by the Rust lane. Read directly by this file:
    `package_dir` (all eight custom-script @is_file gates, spelled `${args.package_dir}`) plus,
    through the merged map, `s3_url` and `package_dir` (shell-command interpolation).
    @ctx::from_args mutates this SAME map in place and returns it as `context`, so the
    `args.package_dir` / `context.package_dir` spellings name one value — the 19-key env
    contract, the `MONGO_LIST`/`REDIS_LIST` → `mongo_list`/`redis_list` decode whose two
    lists this lane feeds the extra engines, and `package_dir`'s untouched pass-through are
    owned by ./../lib/backup_context.sdd.
  @context downstream consumers (this file never reads the lists — it only says which stage
    runs): `restic_args` + `s3_url` (consumed by the backup_init/backup_run/backup_check
    stages), `restic_tags` (backup_run), `secret_list` / `pg_list` / `mysql_list` /
    `mongo_list` / `redis_list` (all five prepare stages — unlike the service twin, every
    decoded engine list has a consumer here), `namespace` (the kubectl `-n` selector of
    ./backup_prepare_redis.rhai), `retention max_*` (backup_prune only — its call is
    commented out), `scale_target` (maintenance_stop TO-DO — unwritten code), while
    `snapshot`, `sub_path`, `base_path` have no reader in the tenant backup lane
    (`deployment_list`/`statefulset_list` live only inside the maintenance TO-DO comments and
    `snapshot` belongs to the ./restore.rhai lane).
  Runtime inputs — eight optional package scripts under `${args.package_dir}/scripts/`:
    `backup.sh` (replaces the whole lane), `backup_prepare.sh` (replaces the five-engine
    prepare block), `backup_prepare_secret.sh`, `backup_prepare_postgresql.sh`,
    `backup_prepare_mysql.sh`, `backup_prepare_mongodb.sh`, `backup_prepare_redis.sh`
    (per-engine replacements) and `backup_before.sh` (an optional hook with NO shipped
    module — file-only). Each gate is pure @is_file on the path literal
    `${args.package_dir}/scripts/<name>`; each executed script is a shell entry,
    not a Rhai module.

Returns:
  Custom-script path: @run hits `return rc` after `backup.sh` succeeds — `rc` there is
    necessarily 0 (a non-zero one threw first) — and the Rust lane discards it.
  Normal path: the implicit value is the trailing `import_run("backup_post", ...)` result (unit
    on a stock image, since `backup_post` ships nowhere); the Rust lane discards this too
    (@common/src/rhaihandler.sdd skip semantics).
  The observable result is entirely side-effect: a restic repository snapshot under
    `context.s3_url`, prepared dumps under `/backup` (the mongo/redis legs contributing
    `mongodb_<name>.archive` and `redis_<name>.rdb`), and the 0-or-throw completion channel
    the exit-4 lane reads.

Raises:
  Exactly eight @throw statements, all the same shape `<script-path> FAILED returning <rc>` —
    template text `${context.package_dir}/scripts/<name> FAILED returning ${rc}` — one per
    custom script (`backup.sh`, `backup_prepare.sh`, `backup_prepare_secret.sh`,
    `backup_prepare_postgresql.sh`, `backup_prepare_mysql.sh`, `backup_prepare_mongodb.sh`,
    `backup_prepare_redis.sh`, `backup_before.sh`) on a non-zero @shell_run code. Throws from
    `backup.sh` onward abort mid-lane; the thrown text reaches the process through the Rust
    lane's `Rhai script error:` prefix, its `Backup of a package failed with:`
    @tracing::error line and exit 4 (frozen by /agent/src/tenant/backup.sdd — no
    `backup_failed` condition, no `set_status_*` marker is minted at this level or by any
    shipped tenant stage).
  Stage re-throws propagate identically: @import_run swallows only the two skip markers
    (`No ${name} module, skipping.` / `No ${name}::run function, skipping.`; owners
    /common/src/rhaihandler.sdd + the vynil-core shim), so a throw escaping a stage aborts
    the run — e.g. `restic check FAILED returning ${rc}` from ./backup_check.rhai,
    `mongodump failed for ${mongo}` from ./backup_prepare_mongodb.rhai, or
    `No running pod found for ${redis} (sts: ${sts})`, `redis SAVE failed for ${redis}`,
    `kubectl cp failed for ${redis}` from ./backup_prepare_redis.rhai.
  Import-time: the module body's sole top-level statement `import "backup_context" as ctx;`
    resolves at module load; a resolution miss is a Rust-lane eval error before @run starts.
    @ctx::from_args itself raises for nothing env-side (./../lib/backup_context.sdd), and
    `context.s3_url` / `context.package_dir` are unguarded reads both always present (the
    former possibly the degraded `s3:/`, which the lane neither detects nor reports — it is
    logged verbatim and left to fail on restic's return codes downstream).

Handles:
  Total-lane custom backup — `backup.sh` present: run it with the repo export, then
    `import_run("backup_post")` and return — skipping every stage (init, maintenance window,
    the five prepare engines, backup_run, backup_check). Absent (the stock case) falls through
    to the full sequence; `backup_pre` still ran before this gate either way.
  Prepare-block routing is file-existence ONLY, never list contents: `backup_prepare.sh`
    present-and-passing bypasses all five engines; otherwise each of
    secret/postgresql/mysql/mongodb/redis takes its own script-or-module branch independently
    and in the fixed secret → postgresql → mysql → mongodb → redis order, the mongodb and
    redis legs nested inside the same `backup_prepare.sh` else-branch as the other three.
    Empty `mongo_list`/`redis_list` (or any empty list) do NOT skip the shipped stages — each
    import_runs and its loop no-ops (`backup_prepare_redis` reads `context.namespace` only
    inside its loop), and ./backup_init.rhai still probes/inits the repository.
  Maintenance window positions: @import_run("maintenance_start") sits right after backup_init
    and before the prepare engines; @import_run("maintenance_stop") after backup_run and
    before backup_check. Both shipped modules are pass-through hook calls around a scale
    TO-DO comment (deployment_list/statefulset_list to 0 / back to `scale_target`): the
    window currently toggles nothing on the cluster, with or without a CR — the CR is not
    even reachable here.
  Unshipped hook names: `backup_pre` and `backup_post` ship in no engine directory
    (./, ./../service, ./../lib) — on a stock image both take the debug-log skip; they exist
    as package `scripts/` slots. `backup_prune` ships in ./ but its ONLY call site is the
    comment `//import_run("backup_prune", context);` between backup_check and backup_post —
    retention envs have no executor in this lane. `backup_before` likewise ships in no
    directory: its gate is the `backup_before.sh` script or nothing.
  RESTIC environment handling — this file exports ONLY `RESTIC_REPOSITORY="${context.s3_url}"`
    (inline `export ...;` prefix before every one of the eight custom scripts);
    `RESTIC_ARGS`-style flags and host identity ride the stages and pod env: `RESTIC_HOST` is
    written only by @backup_context::run at schedule time (./../lib/backup_context.sdd
    `Must`), never read or exported here.
  No cron/schedule branch — correctness here does not depend on any env choosing between
    scheduled and immediate: scheduling lives exclusively in ./schedule_backup.rhai (spec
    pending; its service twin is frozen by ./../service/schedule_backup.sdd); this module,
    reached by a dispatched backup Job, always backs up now.

Must:
  Execute exactly this order with nothing else interleaved: @ctx::from_args(args) → one
    @log_info line `Starting backup using target: ${context.s3_url}` (the only log statement
    at this level) → @import_run("backup_pre") → `backup.sh` gate (run | fall through) →
    @import_run("backup_init") → @import_run("maintenance_start") → `backup_prepare.sh` gate
    (run, OR the secret → postgresql → mysql → mongodb → redis script/stage ladder) →
    `backup_before.sh` gate → @import_run("backup_run") → @import_run("maintenance_stop") →
    @import_run("backup_check") → @import_run("backup_post") → end.
  Ship each custom script's command with the exact prefix
    `export RESTIC_REPOSITORY="${context.s3_url}";` followed by
    `${context.package_dir}/scripts/<name>`, and treat any non-zero @shell_run code as fatal
    at its own throw site (never retried, never collected, `backup.sh` rc 0 alone returning).
  Pass the one `context` map to every @import_run and discard every return — the
    `context = import_run(...)` merge discipline of ./install.sdd is absent here, so stages
    communicate through their own side effects (restic, `/backup`, shell env), never through
    a returned map.
  Resolve every stage name against the four resolver directories frozen by the Rust lane
    ({package_dir}/scripts first, then {config_dir}, {script_dir}/tenant, {script_dir}/lib),
    so a package `scripts/backup_run.rhai` (or any other stage name, including an engine-stage
    script shadowed as a MODULE name) replaces the shipped lane wholesale.
  Keep the import-time surface at the single `import "backup_context" as ctx;` —
    ./../lib/backup_context.rhai executes nothing on load, so module load touches no env,
    filesystem or cluster.
  Keep the prune call commented exactly at `//import_run("backup_prune", context);` — recorded
    behavior: the shipped ./backup_prune.rhai (restic forget with the four keep-* retention
    flags plus --prune) is dead code as wired.
  Keep the flow byte-for-byte shared with ./../service/backup.rhai apart from the two extra
    prepare legs: a reorder, leg addition or throw-text change on one twin must land on both
    in the same edit, with this spec's diff-state claim updated with it.

Must not:
  Write any failure/success marker — no `set_status_*` call, no condition, no tag, no
    `instance` binding, no kube call: the Rust lane never even fetches a @TenantInstance into
    the process, so any status write here would fabricate an object the backup Job never owns.
  Branch on `use_backup`, a cron expression or any env to pick scheduled-vs-immediate:
    the only env influence on this lane is the DECODED env inside @from_args (destination,
    tags, the five engine lists, retention, TLS flag), not a schedule switch.
  Read `context.snapshot` to route backup work — it is decoded here but consumed only by the
    ./restore.rhai lane (by contrast `mongo_list`/`redis_list` DO have consumers here, in
    ./backup_prepare_mongodb.rhai and ./backup_prepare_redis.rhai, so they must not be
    treated as service-lane dead keys).

Depends on:
  ./../lib/backup_context.rhai — the single import; @from_args half of the 19-key env→context
    contract (spec ./../lib/backup_context.sdd, which names this file among the four
    @from_args callers).
  The shipped stage modules of this directory, all specs pending and each self-throwing:
    ./backup_init.rhai (restic cat config, init on rc 10), ./maintenance_start.rhai,
    ./backup_prepare_secret.rhai, ./backup_prepare_postgresql.rhai,
    ./backup_prepare_mysql.rhai, ./backup_prepare_mongodb.rhai (mongodump --archive per
    `mongo_list` entry, oplog-first with no-oplog retry), ./backup_prepare_redis.rhai
    (redis-cli SAVE + kubectl cp `dump.rdb` per `redis_list` entry), ./backup_run.rhai
    (restic backup /backup with --tag ${context.restic_tags}), ./maintenance_stop.rhai,
    ./backup_check.rhai (+ ./backup_prune.rhai, shipped and unwired).
  vynil-core 0.7.7 engine API — the @import_run shim with its two skip markers, @is_file,
    @shell_run (int return code), @log_info (registrars per /common/src/rhaihandler.sdd).

References:
  /agent/src/tenant/backup.sdd — the caller: fixed `backup` snippet, ten-key `args`, the
    four-dir resolver with the hard-coded `tenant` segment, and the exit-4 lane
    (`Backup of a package failed with:`) every throw here lands in.
  ./../service/backup.sdd — the spec twin holding the mirrored open `[?]` decisions. Diff
    state of the sources: the single hunk `@@ -45,6 +45,22 @@` adds the mongodb and redis
    prepare legs to this file and nothing else changes.
  ./restore.rhai — the restore-lane sibling that consumes `snapshot` and the two extra
    engine lists via ./restore_mongodb.rhai and ./restore_redis.rhai (spec pending).
  ./install.sdd — sibling orchestrator style reference: the merge discipline this file drops.
  /agent/tests/rhai_backup_redis.rs — the nearest test file; its mock engine resolves
    scripts/lib + scripts/tenant, tenant-flavored (Tasks).

Scenario: custom backup.sh replaces the whole lane
  Given `${args.package_dir}/scripts/backup.sh` exists in the mounted package scripts
  When @run executes and the script exits 0
  Then the RESTIC_REPOSITORY-exported copy ran, @import_run("backup_post") followed and @run
    returned the rc — backup_init, the maintenance pair, all five prepare engines, backup_run
    and backup_check never ran
  But given the script exits 3
  Then the throw text is `${context.package_dir}/scripts/backup.sh FAILED returning 3` and no
    backup_post import runs

Scenario: prepare ladder order and per-engine replacement over five engines
  Given no `backup_prepare.sh` and no per-engine scripts
  When @run passes the prepare gate
  Then @import_run fires secret → postgresql → mysql → mongodb → redis in that fixed order on
    the one context map, whatever the lists hold (empty lists still import_run, the loops
    no-op)
  Given the same package ships `backup_prepare_mongodb.sh` and `backup_prepare_redis.sh` only
  Then the mongodb and redis legs are the exported shell runs and the other three legs stay
    module imports

Scenario: whole prepare block replaced
  Given `backup_prepare.sh` exists and exits 5
  Then the throw names `backup_prepare.sh FAILED returning 5` with no engine leg — script or
    module — ever running; on exit 0 the flow continues to the backup_before gate

Scenario: stock image skips unshipped hooks and returns via the post-hook
  Given a package with no custom scripts and a stock tenant engine directory set
  When @run completes
  Then `backup_pre` and `backup_post` hit the two debug-log skip markers (they ship nowhere),
    run returns that unit, and the log line `Starting backup using target: s3:/` proves the
    bare-env degraded s3_url is only logged, never validated

Scenario: redis dump aborts the lane mid-prepare
  Given no custom scripts, a `context.redis_list` with one entry, and the redis stage's
    kubectl pod probe answering empty (the shipped stage throws)
  When the ladder reaches the redis leg
  Then `No running pod found for ${redis} (sts: ${sts})` propagates out through @import_run:
    the `backup_before.sh` gate, backup_run, maintenance_stop, backup_check and backup_post
    never run and the Rust lane exits 4 behind `Rhai script error: `
  But given the same package ships `backup_prepare_redis.sh`
  Then the leg is the exported shell run and the shipped module never loads

Scenario: stage throw after backup_run aborts the tail
  Given the sequence reached ./backup_run.rhai and restic backup exits 2
  Then the stage's own throw propagates through @import_run: maintenance_stop, backup_check
    and the backup_post hook never run and the Rust lane exits 4 behind `Rhai script error: `

Scenario: retention envs decide nothing
  Given RESTIC_MAX_DAYLY / WEEKLY / MONTHLY / YEARLY set and no custom script replacing anything
  Then `restic forget` never executes — the only prune caller is the commented
    `//import_run("backup_prune", context);` — and the four decoded `max_*` keys stay unread

