      @Script::new_mock (exactly those two resolver dirs) but no test drives this @run.
      Nearest coverage: the five `backup_redis_*` tests (empty_list_completes, nominal,
      pod_not_found_throws, save_failure_throws, cp_failure_throws) exercise
      ./backup_prepare_redis.rhai — this lane's redis leg — with assertions matching the
      stage's current throw texts; pin them to the redis Scenario above once that stage spec
      exists. The seven `restore_redis_*` tests in the same file target ./restore_redis.rhai,
      NOT a stage of this file — cross-ref their pending specs on ./restore.rhai's spec, not
      here. Zero coverage today for this orchestrator, the other four engine legs and every
      other tenant stage module behind pending specs.
  [?] The maintenance window toggles nothing: ./maintenance_start.rhai and
      ./maintenance_stop.rhai contain only hook passthroughs around a scale TO-DO, so tenant
      dumps run against live workloads — decide whether to implement the
      deployment/statefulset scaling or delete the window (same decision as
      ./../service/backup.sdd; keep the twins in lockstep).
  [?] Prune is commented out while `from_args` decodes the four retention envs — revive the
      `backup_prune` call (after backup_check is the shipped position) or drop the call site
      and its envs from the tenant backup Job contract (same decision as the twin).
  [?] `backup_pre`/`backup_post` ship in no engine directory — package-side hook slots only,
      same posture as ./install.sdd's unshipped hooks; confirm intentional.
  [?] The `backup.sh` replacement also skips backup_check and the maintenance pair and its
      rc-0 return is discarded by Rust — confirm the package-owned-backup semantics (failure
      then requires the package script to exit non-zero) rather than a partial override.
  [?] backup_init runs even when all five engine lists are empty (and on the degraded
      `s3:/`): decide whether init on an envless/degenerate destination should fail fast here
      or keeps riding restic's own rc (which ./backup_init.rhai also ignores unless equal
      to 10).

Done when:
  Every Scenario carries a passing mock-engine test against ./backup.rhai (resolver list
    including scripts/tenant), the frozen order, the five-leg ladder and the eight throw
    texts still match the source, the twin claim still matches
    `diff -u ./../service/backup.rhai ./backup.rhai` (one hunk `@@ -45,6 +45,22 @@`), and
    `specdd lint` is green on this file.
